/-!
# Rudvalis incidence for central coverings

Every prescribed Sylow lies in an actual max4 conjugate. The normalizer
multiplier action is constructed on the actual model and its irreducibility
is reduced to a moved kernel element. The actual max4 core is special of order
2048, with center the marked eight-group and elementary central quotient of
order 256. Its natural and Steinberg module factors use the same quotient
actor, and every outside-core involution has an ambient Sylow-center witness.
This geometry transports to the max4 conjugates used by Sylow placement.
Concrete Sz(8) normalizer geometry and the nontrivial field action on its
multiplier are still needed.

Source: Aschbacher--Smith, I.2.2(7), printed pp.410,412--413.
The conditional results reexported here do not prove the source covering
conclusions, whose assembly belongs to the Chapter I consumer.
-/
